## Gate

Prove one attended v0.2 Claude continuity arrow on an exact candidate:

`omux claude` launches one managed Claude Code authority process -> C1 serves the context with the exact requested model -> C1 returns a provider-originated, explicitly classified pre-body `quota_exhausted` 429 -> the same sidecar elects one distinct provider identity C2 and replays once -> the same Claude process and native context complete with the byte-identical model and no login or restart.

TIN-2721 canonical-keychain mutation is superseded as a product mechanism. It remains historical research only for unmanaged sessions.

## Entry gates

TIN-1759, TIN-1829, TIN-2047, TIN-2400, TIN-2040, TIN-2052, TIN-1803, and the executable exact-candidate proof harness must be accepted. Stage 5 shadow/manual-route proof must pass. The operator must open a finite attended provider-spend window. Synthetic proof never opens this gate.

The existing `Live Provider QA` workflow is v0.1 diagnostic infrastructure only. It is probe-oriented and does not enforce the v0.2 finite request/token/time/currency budget or allowlist-only evidence contract, so it cannot satisfy this gate.

## Required evidence

* two authorized, identity-distinct Claude routes represented only as run-local aliases C1 and C2;
* one locally derived process fingerprint unchanged before, during, and after the arrow, persisted only as a run-local opaque handle;
* `harness_spawn_count == 1`, `harness_restart_count == 0`, and `harness_exec_replacement_count == 0`;
* exact public model identifier byte-identical on both attempts and in the trusted harness-visible result;
* one opaque request handle, exactly two upstream attempts, one alternate, no same-route retry, no third attempt, and no wait beyond the request deadline or 30 seconds;
* context and native-session equality recorded only as booleans/opaque run-local handles;
* no cross-identity replay after body bytes, ambiguity, partial send, cancellation, 5xx, or replay-budget overflow;
* one concurrent managed session remains undisturbed under the accepted shared-lease contract;
* committed allowlist-redacted evidence plus exact GF/Public Source/Release Proof/candidate provenance.

Do not persist raw PIDs, stable identity hashes, account labels, emails, filesystem paths, prompts, responses, bodies, environments, or credentials. Two invocations, two sessions, a manual `/login`, prepared fallback, canonical-keychain mutation, or an out-of-band controller switch do not satisfy this gate.

